# ExaBGP qa/old/5.0/qa/encoding/api-nexthop-self (ExaBGP 685f772e4e): .ci and .msg joined, options spelt option=
option=allowed:the script announces every route with next-hop self, or with next-hop 127.0.0.1, and on this loopback session the speaker's own address is 127.0.0.1, which is also the peer's address; RFC 4271 Section 5.1.3 says "A route originated by a BGP speaker SHALL NOT be advertised to a peer using an address of that peer as NEXT_HOP", so ze withholds every route and logs why (the ExaBGP 6.0 copy, test/exabgp-compat/api/api-nexthop-self.ci, moves the neighbor to 127.0.0.2 for the same reason)
